{
  "id": "holdfast",
  "displayName": "Holdfast",
  "curriculumIndex": 5,
  "teaches": [
    "leadAndDrop",
    "crosshairPlacement",
    "tracking"
  ],
  "_intent": "The big one. Deep woods with a timber keep on each end of the valley, and the whole map is the ground between them. Built for capture the flag: you have to cross it, they have to hold it, and both keeps have a wall you can shoot over and a gate you have to go through. Longest sightlines in the game, and the only map where you are ever attacking a fixed position.",
  "engagementBand": {
    "minMetres": 8.8,
    "targetMedianMetres": 45.76,
    "maxMetres": 84.48,
    "_postureBias": "Measured correction on top of the band-derived posture. 1.0 means the derivation lands it; anything else is geometry having the last word. Set from tools/engagement-report, then re-measure.",
    "postureBias": {
      "range": 1.0,
      "advance": 1.0
    }
  },
  "bounds": {
    "widthMetres": 132.0,
    "lengthMetres": 176.0,
    "heightMetres": 44
  },
  "ground": {
    "colorKey": "ground",
    "thicknessMetres": 1
  },
  "walls": {
    "colorKey": "foliageDeep",
    "heightMetres": 20,
    "transparency": 0,
    "_transparency": "Opaque, not 0.2. Same reasoning as Woods and more of it: these walls were 13220 square metres of semi-transparent surface, by far the largest render cost on any field. The treeline is 31 m and this wall is 20 m, so eleven metres of spire stands above it."
  },
  "navLinkRadiusMetres": 34,
